      "excerpt": "Weather Markets | Kalshi Help Center Copyright (c) 2023, Intercom, Inc. ( [email protected] ) with Reserved Font Name \"Inter\". This Font Software is licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. Copyright (c) 2023, Intercom, Inc. ( [email protected] ) with Reserved Font Name \"Inter\". This Font Software is licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1. Skip to main content Search for articles... All Collections Markets Popular Markets Weather Markets Weather Markets July 22, 2026 Table of contents How do weather markets work? Kalshi offers a wide variety of weather-related markets that allow users to trade contracts based on temperature movements or precipitation amounts in specific cities, from New York City to Los Angeles. Traders can take positions on whether a city will reach a certain high temperature or fall within a particular range. Each weather market names its official settlement source in its market rules. Daily high/low temperature markets settle based on the final climate report issued by the National Weather Service (NWS), typically released the following morning. Hourly temperature markets settle on readings from The Weather Company . Always check the specific market\u2019s rules for its source. How Do I Trade on Weather Markets? Kalshi creates a prediction market around a specific temperature threshold for a given location. For example: \u201cHighest temperature in Chicago on April 15, 2025?\u201d \u200b Contract prices for temperature ranges may shift as new weather data (e.g., forecasts, model runs, satellite images, observations) becomes available. Note: Not "
